.TH DIPISCAN 1 "2026-08-17" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipiscan \- scan and report on DVB-IPI multicast streams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipiscan
[\fIoptions\fR] 1>\fIplaylist\fR 2>\fIlog\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipiscan
sweeps a multicast /24 (or the analogous IPv6 range) for DVB-IPI services
and writes a playlist of what answered. Every address/port combination in
the configured range is probed once; each probe joins the multicast group
(directly via IGMP/MLD, or through a udpxy gateway) and waits for a PAT
and SDT service name within the configured time budget.
.PP
This tool exists because deployments do not always use DVBSTP/SD&S
service discovery as implemented by
.BR dipisds (1).
Where SD&S is available, scanning a live multicast range for services is
unnecessary; \fBdipiscan\fR fills the gap when it is not.
.PP
Output can be written as an M3U playlist, XSPF playlist, a local CSV
format, SD&S Broadcast Discovery XML (ETSI TS 102 034), or discarded
entirely (only the stderr log remains). The M3U, XSPF, and CSV formats
are convenience additions and are not part of the DVB-IPI specification.
Every format also carries the DVB triplet (transport_stream_id,
original_network_id, service_id) read from PAT/SDT.
.PP
By default one address is reported as one program: whichever program's
PMT resolves first. With \fB\-M\fR, every program listed in the PAT at
that address gets its own playlist entry.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mcast " \fIaddr\fR"
Base multicast group, IPv4 or IPv6; the last byte is swept 1..254.
Default: 239.19.75.0.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIport\fR[\-\fIport\fR]"
Port or inclusive port range. Default: 8700.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fIfmt\fR"
Output format: m3u, csv, xspf, xml, or null. Default: m3u.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-provider " \fIname\fR"
DomainName for the output. Required when \fB\-f xml\fR is used.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out " \fIpath\fR"
Output file, or "\-" for stdout. Default: stdout.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " \fIsecs\fR"
Wall-clock time budget per candidate. Default: 1.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-mpts
Report every program found at an address, not just the first. Waits out
the whole timeout budget per address.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-udpxy " \fIip\fR:\fIport\fR"
Probe through a udpxy gateway instead of a direct IGMP/MLD join.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-iface " \fIiface\fR"
Interface to use for the multicast join. Default: kernel default route.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print per-candidate diagnostics on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fIwhen\fR
Control colored output: auto, always, or never. Default: auto.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipiscan \-m 239.19.75.0 \-p 8700-8705 >hd.m3u
Scan a custom address/port range, write an M3U playlist to a file.
.TP
.B dipiscan \-v \-f csv \-o scan.csv
Scan with per-candidate diagnostics on stderr, write CSV output.
.TP
.B dipiscan \-u 127.0.0.1:8080 \-m 239.19.75.0 \-f xspf >playlist.xspf
Scan through a udpxy gateway, write an XSPF playlist.
.TP
.B dipiscan \-f xml \-P example.org \-o scan.xml
Write SD&S Broadcast Discovery XML, ready to feed into \fBdipisds \-a \-i\fR.
.TP
.B dipiscan \-M \-t 3 \-f xml \-P example.org \-o scan.xml
MPTS-aware scan: one row per program per address, with a raised timeout
budget to allow every PAT-listed program to be named.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B nonzero
Argument error, or I/O or network failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipisds (1),
.BR dipirec (1)
.PP
